<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rassemblement Démocratique Africain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1946</span> · Also known as African Democratic Rally, RDA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rassemblement Démocratique Africain was an inter-territorial political movement founded at a congress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamako">Bamako</a> in October 1946 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-houphouet-boigny">Félix Houphouët-Boigny</a>. It had branches in most territories of French West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-equatorial-africa">Equatorial Africa</a> and campaigned for African rights within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-union">French Union</a>. Its sections, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-uganda">Democratic Party</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> and the Sudanese Union, led several countries to independence.</p></div>
